problem: Add source-install support to install.sh while preserving release-download behavior
approach: Rewrote the installer for clarity, added --from-source plus repo auto-detection, and verified syntax/help plus a default in-repo source install to a temp dir
failed_paths:
  - None
verification:
  - bash -n install.sh
  - ./install.sh --help
  - ./install.sh --dir "$(mktemp -d)"
workflow_learning: For shell installers with dual local/remote behavior, detect the local checkout from script location and git metadata before changing defaults
related_files:
  - install.sh
